I happen to know an item merchant
who might be able to help

159
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:29,530
us out

160
00:12:29,613 --> 00:12:36,160
thanks

161
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:37,717
my man come back

162
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:41,417
anytime yeah whatever looks

163
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:43,797
like you're still running all
the suckers down with those hard

164
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:49,197
deals of yours no way kirito
buy cheap and sell cheap that's

165
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,877
my motto i'm a businessman you
know that that's selling cheap

166
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:56,077
parts a lie though don't go
slandering my good name brother

167
00:12:56,160 --> 00:13:02,517
what the hell has gotten into
you you're supposed to be a solo

168
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:08,417
player man what are you doing
hanging around with Asuna his

169
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:13,737
HP dropped a zero in a safe
zone you sure it wasn't a duel

170
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:18,197
well no one saw a winner icon
we can also rule out the murder

171
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:21,917
being asleep PK he was walking
with Yoriko before it happened

172
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,597
and besides his death was too
elaborate to be some random duel.

173
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:28,077
The PKer who did this had it planned out.

174
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:29,537
We're pretty sure of that.

175
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:31,540
And then there's this.

176
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:47,017
A player made this. Really? Who
was it? Can you tell? Grimlock.

177
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,806
Never heard that name before.

178
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:51,717
It's not one of the top
blacksmiths, that's for damn sure.

179
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:54,357
Far as I can tell, there's
nothing Special about this,

180
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:56,557
yeah, but it's something to go on, right?

181
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,957
MM—Hmm, is there?

182
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:01,497
Like an item name listed,
you'll love it: guilty thorn.

183
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:03,577
There's a name for you.

184
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:05,417
It kind of fits, though—don't you think?

185
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:08,737
Seriously, guilty thorn!

186
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:10,240
guilty thorn

187
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:20,880
Here goes.

188
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:24,810
Wait, stop!

189
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,477
What's the matter?

190
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,097
What do you mean, what's the matter?

191
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,651
Are you out of your mind?

192
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:34,797
That thing's already killed one person!

193
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:38,477
I know, but we need to find out what
this thing's capable of, don't we?

194
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,501
Would you stop being so reckless?

195
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,306
