if you had ever heard the name Grimlock.

198
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,757
Yes, I have.

199
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:11,075
Actually, until a few months ago, he
was in the guild with me and Caynz.

200
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:15,857
Listen, we took the spear that
impaled Caynz to an appraiser.

201
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:20,293
We had him go over it pretty carefully,
and we found out Grimlock made it.

202
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:24,600
Can you think of any reason why you did?

203
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:28,740
Yes, I can.

204
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:32,477
I should have told you
everything yesterday.

205
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:34,917
It's just, I couldn't.

206
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,100
It's something I've been
trying very hard to forget.

207
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,920
But now, I have no choice.

208
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:46,700
I should tell you about
how my guild was destroyed.

209
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:54,440
When we formed it, Golden
Apple was the name we chose.

210
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:59,080
Six months ago, we killed a rare monster.

211
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:03,340
It dropped a powerful ring that
raised a player's agility by 20.

212
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,217
Some of us wanted to
keep it for the guild,

213
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:10,124
others wanted to sell it
and split the earnings.

214
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:14,380
We couldn't agree and in the
end, we put it to a vote.

215
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:18,280
It was five to three
in favor of selling it.

216
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:23,620
Our leader, Griselda, took it to
a large town on the front lines.

217
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:27,766
She was going to sell it to a
broker and was staying overnight.

218
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:32,380
We waited and waited,
but she never came back.

219
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:37,280
It wasn't till later.

220
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:39,912
We learned our worst fears had come true.

221
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,099
Griselda was dead.

222
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:45,420
To this day, I still
don't know how she died.

223
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:49,277
No one's gonna leave a safe
zone with a rare item like that.

224
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:50,200
Too risky.

225
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:53,357
You think someone could've
pulled a sleep PK on her?

226
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,146
Not if it was six months ago.

227
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:57,222
That method's still sort of new.

228
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:58,250
You're right.

229
00:16:58,333 --> 00:17:00,455
But she wasn't a random victim either.

230
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,677
No, the killer was after the ring.

231
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:05,172
It has to be someone who knew she had it.

232
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:06,430
Which means?

233
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:09,800
The killer is one of the
seven others in our guild.

234
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:11,110
Yes.

235
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:13,240
We have our suspects.

236
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:16,517
Now we just have to figure out
who didn't want to sell the ring.

237
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:19,697
I doubt the killer waited till
after Griselda sold the ring.

238
00:17:19,780 --> 00:17:21,617
She was killed before she sold it.

239
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:22,641
That's my guess.

240
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:23,610
Probably.

241
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:26,277
Tell us what you know about Grimlock.

242
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:29,536
Well, I guess for starters,
he was Griselda's husband.

243
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:31,300
Oh, but not in real life.

244
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:32,540
Just in the game.

245
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:35,980
Griselda was a powerful Swordsman.

246
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:38,820
She was beautiful and smart.

247
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:44,219
Grimlock was kind, and I can't
remember a day when he wasn't smiling.

248
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:48,071
They made a great couple and
got along as husband and wife.

249
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:52,417
If Grimlock is really the one
who murdered Caynz yesterday,

250
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:55,577
then he's probably going
after the three guild

251
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:58,189
members who voted
against selling the ring.

252
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:03,597
Caynz was one of the three who wanted
to keep their reign for the guild.

253
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,856
I was the other one.

254
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:07,427
Then who's the third person?

255
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:09,461
The other's a tank named Schmidt.

256
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:14,404
And he, the last I heard, is on the front
lines now with the Holy Dragon Alliance.

257
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:15,630
Schmidt, huh?

258
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,607
I've heard that name before.

259
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:20,937
He's leader of the defense unit
of the Holy Dragon Alliance.

260
00:18:21,020 --> 00:18:22,620
He's an exceptional lancer.

261
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,060
Oh yeah, him.

262
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,701
Wait, do you really know Schmidt?

263
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:31,257
Well, I've run into him a couple
times while clearing bosses, so...

264
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,717
I need to see him right away.

265
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,237
Could you please take me to him?

266
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:37,637
If he's on the front lines, he
probably hasn't heard about the murder.

267
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:41,800
He needs to know before what
happened to Caynz happens to him.

268
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:46,497
We'll help you get in touch with Schmidt.

269
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:48,917
I know someone in the
Holy Dragon Alliance.

270
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,059
He'll help us out.

271
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:51,455
We'll visit their HQ.

272
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:55,428
Okay, but first we should make
sure she gets back to the inn.

273
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,896
Yoriko, you have to stay there, okay?

274
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:00,997
Seriously, don't go
anywhere until we get back.

275
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:01,910
All right.

276
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:12,077
Okay, so how do you think a murder
like this happened in a safe zone?

277
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,219
I can see three ways it could have.

278
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:17,459
Right off the bat, it's
possible it was a fair duel.

279
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:20,677
Or maybe someone took
advantage of a bug that

280
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,677
combines a bunch of
different kill methods.

281
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,584
Yeah, I can see that happening.

282
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:25,780
And the third?

283
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:29,836
Use something to bypass the
protection of a safe zone.

284
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,078
Some kind of skill or maybe an item.

285
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:35,720
No, on second thought, that
third idea is impossible.

286
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:37,060
What do you mean?

287
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:38,476
Because it's unfair.

288
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,251
I kind of hate to admit it, but it's true.

289
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:45,321
The rules of SAO are essentially
fair for every player in the game.

290
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:49,280
So there's no way the game would
allow murders in safe zones.

291
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:52,040
I see.

292
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:01,160
So that's what killed Caynz,

293
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:04,752
and you're sure about the
spear, was it really Grimlock's?

294
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
There's no doubt.

295
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,941
But then why would he wait
six months to kill him?

296
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:13,617
Unless, wait, could he
have stolen the ring?

297
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:16,994
Do you think it's possible
he killed Griselda after all?

298
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:19,657
Does Grimlock want to kill the three of us

299
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:21,997
because we didn't want
to sell the damn ring?

300
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:24,117
Is that why he's after you and me now?

301
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:27,557
Maybe Grimlock made the spear
for someone else from our guild,

302
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:30,137
and maybe they're the
ones who killed Caynz.

303
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:31,577
Or maybe...

304
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:34,836
Griselda's come back from
the dead to get her revenge.

305
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:38,297
A player can't kill another
player inside a safe zone,

306
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:40,960
but something else like a ghost could.

307
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:47,600
I couldn't sleep at all last
night, so I stayed up thinking.

308
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:50,432
It was everyone's fault!

309
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:52,357
Everyone in the guild is guilty!

310
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,205
Her blood is on all our hands!

311
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:57,197
Our fate was sealed
when that ring dropped!

312
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:58,297
We shouldn't have voted!

313
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:01,560
We should have done whatever
Griselda told us to do!

314
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:09,060
Grimlock was the only one,
the only member of the guild,

315
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:12,301
who said we should leave
the decision to Griselda.

316
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:14,130
You see?

317
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:17,037
He's the only one of us
who can avenge Griselda.

318
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:21,002
He's the only member of our guild
who has the right to avenge her.

319
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,737
You gotta be kidding.

320
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:25,600
You gotta be kidding. Why now?

321
00:21:25,940 --> 00:21:28,580
After all this time, why kill us now?

322
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:31,759
You can't be okay with this, Yurko!

323
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:35,352
How can you accept being killed
over some stupid vendetta?

324
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:56,897
You gotta go!

325
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:58,957
Let's

326
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:06,040
go!

327
00:22:43,260 --> 00:22:44,337
Thank

328
00:22:44,420 --> 00:22:45,497
you

329
00:22:45,580 --> 00:22:52,580
so

330
00:22:56,220 --> 00:22:57,279
much for watching.

331
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,577
Thank

332
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:11,977
you

333
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:19,060
so

334
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:26,897
much for watching.
